{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Feathering a Composite Edge.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Feathering a Composite Edge.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"feathering a composite edge feathering a composite edge","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Feathering a Composite Edge.md","fileName":"Feathering a Composite Edge.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Feathering a Composite Edge","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-15 18:17\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Compositing and Keying]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Compositing and Keying","Sky Augmentation versus Extraction","digitalvisualeffectsandcompositing.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Feathering a Composite Edge.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Feathering a Composite Edge.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"feathering a composite edge feathering a composite edge","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Feathering a Composite Edge.md","fileName":"Feathering a Composite Edge.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Feathering a Composite Edge","heading":"Feathering a Composite Edge","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A hard-edged matte can reveal where two photographed plates meet. Feathering or alpha blur turns that abrupt boundary into a gradual mixture and can hide minor differences in the edge position. The book's sky-augmentation example begins with a large rectangular mask that visibly cuts across the sky; a modest edge feather makes the join less conspicuous. Feathering does not repair wrong light direction, color, or perspective, so those cues must also be checked. See [[Sky Augmentation versus Extraction]].","tags":["baby"],"links":["Compositing and Keying","Sky Augmentation versus Extraction","digitalvisualeffectsandcompositing.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":